### How it works (summary)

| Trigger event | What fires in `Opportunities` | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `before insert` | `onBeforeInsert()` (then `onAfterInsert()`) | Defaults `CloseDate` → today + 30 days; defaults `Type` → `'New Customer'` if not already set |
| `before / after update` | no override → base-class no-ops | No defaults applied (per requirement) |
| all other events | base-class no-ops | No-ops |

* `this.records` is the `List<SObject>` supplied by the framework (trigger `new` context on insert).  
* `super.onBeforeInsert()` is called to let any validation / cross-trigger logic in the base class run first.  
* `Type` is null-checked (`== null`) rather than checked against `'Prospecting'` (the field default) so an API / Data-Loader caller that explicitly passed a value keeps it intact.

