|---|---|
| Reactivity | `@api status` is a reactive property; the parent can set it at any time and the child re-renders. The two getters (`hasStatus`, `badgeClass`) depend on `status`, so they are re-evaluated on every re-render. |
| Conditional rendering | `lwc:if={hasStatus}` / `lwc:else` on sibling `<template>` elements — exactly one branch is in the DOM at a time. When `status` is `""`, `null`, or `undefined`, `hasStatus` is falsy and only the `<p>` renders; otherwise the `<span>` renders. |
| Theme class | The `badgeClass` getter builds the full class string (`"slds-badge slds-theme_info"`, etc.). Unknown statuses get `"slds-badge"` with no theme class. |
| Directive compliance | Uses `lwc:if` / `lwc:else` on `<template>` wrappers (not the deprecated `if:true`/`if:false`). |

