public class HouseholdService {

    public static Id createHousehold(List<Contact> members) {

        if (members == null || members.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('members must not be null or empty');
        }

        // Resolve the household record-type Id dynamically – never hard-code it.
        Id hhRtId = Schema.SObjectType.Account.getRecordTypeInfosByDeveloperName()
            .get('HH_Account')
            .getRecordTypeId();

        // 1. Create the household Account.
        //    Name is intentionally left blank so NPSP auto-generates it + greetings.
        Account hh = new Account();
        hh.RecordTypeId = hhRtId;
        insert hh;

        // 2. Associate every new contact with the household, then insert in one DML.
        for (Contact c : members) {
            c.AccountId = hh.Id;
        }
        insert members;

        // 3. Set the first contact as the household's primary contact.
        //    Use a fresh SObject so we touch only that one field and don't
        //    accidentally overwrite anything a trigger may have changed on
        //    the Account during the Contact insert.
        update new Account(
            Id = hh.Id,
            npe01__One2OneContact__c = members[0].Id
        );

        return hh.Id;
    }
}
```

**Design notes**

| Concern | How it is handled |
|---|---|
| **No hard-coded Record Type Id** | Resolved at runtime via `getRecordTypeInfosByDeveloperName().get('HH_Account')`. |
| **NPSP auto-naming / greetings** | `Account.Name` is never assigned; the `HH_Account` record type plus the absence of a manual name lets NPSP's `npe01` code generate the household name and greeting. |
| **Single household, no orphans** | The entire method runs in one transaction. If any DML (`insert members`, `update`) throws, the unhandled exception rolls back the whole transaction—including the initial `insert hh`—so no empty or stray household Account can survive. |
| **Primary-contact reference** | Set in a separate `update` on a *new* `Account(Id = …)` SObject that carries only `npe01__One2OneContact__c`, preventing an accidental overwrite of any field a Contact-trigger may have already modified on the Account. |
| **`IllegalArgumentException`** | Thrown immediately when `members` is `null` or empty, before any DML. |

