## Explanation

The `orgPreferences` block (with its `enabled`/`disabled` arrays) was removed from the scratch-org definition schema. Modern `sf org create scratch` expects org-level feature toggles to be expressed under a `settings` key whose structure mirrors the Metadata API `settings/<Type>.settings` files.

Mapping of each legacy preference to its Metadata-API equivalent:

| Legacy `orgPreferences` entry | Modern `settings` equivalent |
|---|---|
| `S1DesktopEnabled` (enabled) | `lightningExperienceSettings.enableS1DesktopEnabled: true` |
| `ChatterEnabled` (enabled) | `chatterSettings.enableFeedEnabled: true` |
| `NetworksEnabled` (enabled) | Covered by `features: ["Communities"]` (kept as-is) |
| `Translation` (enabled) | `translationSettings.enableTranslation: true` |
| `S1EncryptedStoragePref2` (disabled) | `encryptionSettings.enableEncryptedStorage: false` |

`NetworksEnabled` has no standalone `settings` key in the current schema; enabling Digital Experiences is achieved by listing `"Communities"` in the `features` array, which is already present and preserved per the requirement to keep `features` unchanged.

